  "term": "amitriptyline",
  "definition": "Amitriptyline is a tricyclic antidepressant with sedating and anticholinergic effects. It appears to work by reducing the reuptake of norepinephrine and serotonin at nerve endings, which increases their activity, and it also seems to block some cholinergic and alpha-1 adrenergic responses.",
